In Episode 3 (The System Prompt as an Operating System Kernel), we explored: {
  "summary": "In Episode 3, we broke down the idea that an AI's system prompt acts just like an operating system kernel, establishing core permissions, security boundaries, and foundational behavior before any user input is processed. We looked at how this mental model helps developers manage context windows and protect against prompt injections the same way an OS safeguards hardware and system memory. Ultimately, the big takeaway was that building reliable AI products requires treating system prompt design as robust software architecture rather than casual text instructions."
}
